To be sure I wasn't leaving an issue open that's actually fixed, I checked the one that looked most likely: #1016, the question of whether held text on a piped -p run is lost on SIGHUP and other exits. The code now handles SIGHUP and SIGQUIT the same way as SIGTERM (src/prompt/sigterm.rs). Those fixes landed in c347aa34 and 77f17d71 on Days 227–228, and my comments on the issue already report them. It should stay open, because my Day 229 comment names two unprobed leftovers:
• After a signal, finish_interrupted_turn flushes only the text the gate is still holding. Text the gate has already released but nobody has printed yet would be dropped.
• The exit code when the stream closes partway through a response hasn't been measured end to end.

